  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The loop (ADR-0026, 0027, 0028)",
      "items": [
        "A loop is Shape, Realize, Check, Ship; LOOP_STAGES in packages/core/src/lifecycle.ts is the one list.",
        "Its status goes PROPOSED, OPEN, CLOSED; the loops function is its one writer (backend/amplify/functions/loops/handler.ts) and logs each change in Activity.",
        "claude.ai proposes a loop with its brief, drafts a retrospective and hands over stories as DRAFTs (functions/mcp/tools.ts). Starting, moving and closing are a person's acts, refused for the chat, the edge and agents (loops/policy.ts).",
        "A new loop starts only when every earlier one is CLOSED, with an outcome (shipped fully, shipped partially, not shipped, cancelled) and its retrospective."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Who may write what",
      "items": [
        "AppSync's group rules let a member read their workspace's rows and create their own Message, Story draft, Decision and Issue (backend/amplify/data/resource.ts). The runs function approves a run and accepts a story, a person's acts (functions/runs/handler.ts).",
        "A field marked read-only (phase, status, outcome, approvedBy, acceptedBy) is written only by its function.",
        "Organizations and workspaces, with their Cognito groups and their copied tenantName, are written by adminUsers alone (ADR-0024, ADR-0030).",
        "Shopify is written only by execute, one approved step at a time, with the key it reads from Secrets Manager; Odoo is only read, by connections (ADR-0023, functions/execute/handler.ts, functions/connections/handler.ts)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Knowledge and secrets",
      "items": [
        "Each workspace's object, its knowledge graphs and its documents, lives in S3 behind objectProxy, which checks the group and hands out a presigned URL; a write needs the current ETag (functions/objectProxy).",
        "The shared workspace is the organization's second brain, read by every member.",
        "System keys and team-channel webhooks go into Secrets Manager under ovs/<workspace>/…, never into S3 or a row, and are never returned (functions/connections, functions/notify/channelHandler.ts)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Talk and the team channel (ADR-0029)",
      "items": [
        "Messages live in threads: room:<workspace>, loop:<id> and story:<id>; Presence says who is here.",
        "The notify function reads the Activity and Message streams and posts one line per event to the workspace's Discord, Slack or Teams webhook, for the categories chosen (functions/notify/handler.ts). Nothing comes back in.",
        "claude.ai connects with one URL: the MCP server answers its registration with the public ovs-claude client (ADR-0030, functions/mcp/protocol.ts)."
      ]
    }
  ]
